indications_limitations:
&lt;p&gt; The intraoperative ventricular mapping procedure is covered under Medicare only for the uses and medical conditions described below:&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt; 
&lt;li&gt; Localize accessory pathways associated with the Wolff-Parkinson-White (WPW) and other preexcitation syndromes;&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Map the sequence of atrial and ventricular activation for drug-resistant supraventricular tachycardias;&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Delineate the anatomical course of His bundle and&sol;or bundle branches during corrective cardiac surgery for congenital heart diseases; and&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Direct the surgical treatment of patients with refractory ventricular tachyarrhythmias.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
